From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:21:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: mtk_wdt: stop a watchdog running from boot
 across suspend

With WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED and no user of /dev/watchdog, the
core keeps a watchdog the bootloader left running alive with its own
worker (WDOG_HW_RUNNING). mtk_wdt_suspend() stops the hardware only
when the watchdog is active, so such a watchdog keeps counting through
a system suspend in which no CPU runs that worker. On MT6797 the 31 s
timeout then resets the system during any suspend longer than about
15 s past the last kick.

Stop and restart the hardware for a watchdog that is running from boot
as well. The core still owns it after resume and keeps kicking it.
---
 drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
index 9ee35ef1d..2ac5e4d97 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/mtk_wdt.c
@@ -854,7 +854,12 @@ static int mtk_wdt_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct mtk_wdt_dev *mtk_wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev))
+	/*
+	 * A watchdog left running from boot, which the core keeps alive with
+	 * no user, keeps counting in a suspend where no CPU runs that kick.
+	 */
+	if (watchdog_active(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev) ||
+	    watchdog_hw_running(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev))
 		mtk_wdt_stop(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -864,7 +869,8 @@ static int mtk_wdt_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct mtk_wdt_dev *mtk_wdt = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (watchdog_active(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev)) {
+	if (watchdog_active(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev) ||
+	    watchdog_hw_running(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev)) {
 		mtk_wdt_start(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev);
 		mtk_wdt_ping(&mtk_wdt->wdt_dev);
 	}
